            <ArticleTitle>Esters as Alkynyl Acyl Ammonium and Azolium Precursors: A Formal [2 + 3] Annulation with Amidomalonates via Lewis Base/Lewis Acid Cooperative Catalysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6724-6727</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03453</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Esters are for the first time used as α,β-unsaturated alkynyl acyl ammonium and azolium precursors to undergo a formal [2 + 3] annulation with amidomalonates through DMAP/LiCl or carbene/LiCl cooperative catalysis. A wide range of (Z)-5-amino-3-furanones were obtained in moderate to high yields with high regioselectivity and stereoselectivity. In addition, a plausible mechanism based on the calculated charge distribution of the intermediates is proposed to explain the regioselectivity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
